Drop reclaim's reference check: unlink every path the row names, whether or not another row names
it too (MEMNG-959).

Two memo rows pointed at ONE original then lose it on the first delete — the second memo's picture
is gone while its row still promises it. The probes that must turn red are the two delete orders of
the `same-path` shape. The `staged` shape stays green on purpose: a staging hit gives each row its
own hard-linked name, which no reference count is needed to protect, and that is the property the
staged cases pin.

